  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% figure but only as a trigger for corrective action: models above it can keep selling, sales stop only at regulator discretion, and per-model results go to customers but not the public, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which forces Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) to recall. S3 gives a six-year retrofit window with a where-feasible escape, and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months, which delays Halcyon's higher suppression cost."
 },
